  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>P: By <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> F is in +y<br >Q: By <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> F is in +ve x.<br >R: By <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> , F is in +ve y<br >By <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> , F is in -ve y<br >But later has more magnitude, since its closer to (0, b). Therefore net force is in - y<br >S: By <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> , F is in +ve x and by <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> , F is in -x, but later is more in magnitude, since its closer to (0, b). Therefore net force is in -ve x.<br ><br/><img src=\"assets\\st0028_d5e1a40d3491.png\"/></p>"
